docs {
  # Put Vehicle Detail By ID

  This request is used to update a vehicle by using given `ID`. The updated fields are `vehicle_name`, `vehicle_merk`, `vehicle_type`, `vehicle_price`, `vehicle_distance`, `vehicle_category`, `vehicle_status`, `vehicle_year_made`, `vehicle_plate_number`, `vehicle_fuel_status`, `vehicle_default_fuel`, `vehicle_color`, `vehicle_transmission`, and `vehicle_capacity`. This request interacts with the MySQL database, has a protected routes, and audited activity (history).

  ## Path Parameters

  | Name | Type   | Required | Description | Example                               |
  |------|--------|----------|--------------|------------------------------------------|
  | id   | string | yes      | Vehicle ID  | 4f33d5e4-de9f-11ed-b5ea-0242ac120002   |

  ## Responses

  **200 — Vehicle update successfully**
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "vehicle updated"
  }
```

  **400 — Validation failed** (one of the following)
```json
  { "status": "failed", "message": "vehicle name must be at least 2 characters" }
```
```json
  { "status": "failed", "message": "vehicle type is a required field" }
```
```json
  { "status": "failed", "message": "vehicle type must be one of the following values City Car, Minibus, Motorcycle, Hatchback, Sedan, SUV, Pickup Truck, Convertible, Coupe, Van, Wagon, Crossover, Electric" }
```

  **404 — vehicle failed to fetched**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "vehicle not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}